    <h2 class="reveal">The hardest question isn't what you can do. It's what you shouldn't do.</h2>
    <div class="lead-text reveal">
      <p>As a company gains customers, funding and new opportunities, complexity grows fast. Research shows that many startups fail because of:</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="dot-list reveal">
      <li>Lack of product-market fit</li>
      <li>Premature scaling</li>
      <li>Misallocated resources</li>
      <li>Too many initiatives</li>
      <li>Weak prioritisation</li>
      <li>Organisational complexity</li>
      <li>Poor investment decisions</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="lead-text reveal">
      <p>Lack of capital is rarely the root problem. <strong>The money runs out because it was invested in the wrong things.</strong></p>
      <p><small>CB Insights, Startup Genome and McKinsey &amp; Company describe these as recurring reasons why startups and scaleups fail.</small></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

